  "prefLabel": "Env-A 1203.21 Letterpress printing",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Env-A 1203.21 “Letterpress printing” means a printing process in which the image area is raised relative to the non-image area and the paste ink is transferred to the substrate directly from the image surface.\n\nSource. (See Revision Note at chapter heading for Env-A 1200) #9933, eff 6-1-11; ss by #12899, eff 10-17-19",
